From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: use duelist helpers in libduel.cpp

Validity checks: 101 lines `p != 0 && p != 1` (and `tp > 1`, `p != 0 && p != 1 && p != PLAYER_ALL`) now use `is_duelist(p)`. The variable is the same and the accept set stays {0, 1} with 2 duelists. The check that accepts PLAYER_ALL keeps `&& p != PLAYER_ALL`.
Opponent: 12 `1 - x` now use `opponent_of(x)`. Each x is 0 or 1 at that site (after a duelist check, or infos.turn_player), and the result goes to a uint8_t.
Loops and arrays: 2 loops `p < 2` use `n_duelists`. 4 local arrays `[2]` indexed by a duelist are `[MAX_DUELISTS]`, with explicit initial values. 2 explicit pairs (player 0 then player 1) became loops in the same order.
Same with 2 duelists: all values and the order of statements are the same.

Left unchanged: 3 decision sites (Win check, GetBattleMonster relative pair, 1 - returns.at), PLAYER_NONE and PLAYER_ALL sites (phase 2), and non-player `< 2`, `[0]`, `[1]` uses. See unchanged-sites.md.
---
 libduel.cpp | 254 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------
 1 file changed, 127 insertions(+), 127 deletions(-)

